  "description": "Fuselage: White upper fuselage; navy lower fuselage and belly. Cheatlines: A red pinstripe over a thin white line at the white/navy split, which runs level well below the windows and curves down to the belly just behind the radome and under the tail cone. Tail: Navy fin with lighter-blue horizontal bands, a red cap over a thin white line, and the white US Airways flag (square and five bars) mid-fin. Engines: Navy cowlings, bare inlet lips. Winglets: Navy wingtip fences with a small white flag. Titles: American's standard 'American' and flight symbol forward. Artwork: none. Colors hex: matched by eye from photos.",
