  "notes": "Drawn from right-side photos only (no dated left-side photo on Commons); the scheme is taken as symmetric. Heights are measured against the fuselage's outline in the photos. Faint lighter-gray bands show on the aft fuselage in some light (a ghost of the fin stripes); too faint to place, not drawn. The fin's band count and spacing are approximate. Whether the fin flag's square sits forward or aft on the left side is not seen (on the right it's aft). The belly under the wing box is navy as far as the 2021 view from below shows. Re-checked 2026-11-15: 'American' about x 0.18-0.28, read against the doors on N578UW (right side, 2026-10-20, a steep three-quarter view) and agreeing with the side-on A321 heritage jets; the split's sweeps down at the nose and the tail drawn as curves. No measured A321 shape yet."
